From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Kamil=20Postro=C5=BCny?= <kamil@postrozny.pl>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 21:17:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] kk: MESA_KK_DEBUG=passes counts encoders, barriers and passes
 a frame

KosmicKrisp encodes each Vulkan command as it comes: a render pass is
one Metal render encoder or more, every encoder ends on an all-stages
barrier, and nothing folds, merges or drops work between passes. DXMT
plans a whole encoder list first (dxmt_context.cpp,
checkEncoderRelation) and counts what it saved per frame
(render_pass_optimized, clear_pass_optimized). To tell whether rules
of that kind would save anything on KosmicKrisp, the driver must say
what a frame records.

With MESA_KK_DEBUG=passes the queue logs, about once a second and at
its end, a [kk-passes] line: the interval's totals and their mean per
presented frame of command buffers, render passes, render and compute
encoders, Metal draws, render encoders ended without a draw, clear-only
passes, encoder-end barriers, pipeline barriers by where they fall (in
a render encoder, splitting it, in a compute encoder, with no encoder),
and render encoders ended for compute work. It also counts the passes
DXMT's rules would apply to, within one command buffer:

- fold-cand: a clear-only pass, then with no encoder between, a pass
  that loads an attachment subresource the first cleared;
- merge-cand: a pass, then with no encoder or barrier between, one with
  the same attachments, area and layers that loads all of them and
  whose predecessor stored all of them;
- dead-ds-direct / dead-ds-later: a depth or stencil aspect a pass
  stored that the next pass using it clears or discards on its whole
  area, with no encoder between or with encoders between (whose reads,
  if any, are not seen, so this one is an upper bound).

Without the flag nothing is counted or kept and the encoded commands
are unchanged.

Linear: PLA-72
Class: diagnostics
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-22-vulkan-perf-resume.md
Offered-upstream: no
